course: dictionary
lesson: 11540
title: Altitude: how high is it?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Altitude tells you how high something is above the level of the sea or above the ground. A mountain, a town or a plane can each have an altitude. «The plane flew at a high altitude, above the clouds.» Here the plane is very high up.
explain: Read the words around altitude to find its meaning. «As the car climbed the mountain road, its altitude rose.» Rose means went up, so altitude must mean how high the car is. Check by swapping in your meaning: "how high the car is" still makes sense.
explain: Altitude also has a maths meaning. In a triangle, the altitude is the straight line that goes down from one corner to the opposite side, at a right angle. Its length is the height of the triangle. Maths and geography use the same idea: how high something is.
fact: Altitude means how high something is above the sea or the ground.
fact: «At high altitude» means very high up, such as on a mountain or in a plane.
fact: Air gets thinner and colder at high altitude.
fact: In maths, the altitude of a triangle is the height: a line straight down from a corner, at a right angle, to the opposite side.
fact: «Altitude sickness» is when you feel unwell because you are very high up.
exercise: «The plane flew at a high altitude above the clouds.» What does altitude mean here? | *How high the plane is above the ground | How many people are on board | How heavy the plane is | How fast the plane goes
exercise: «Air gets thinner and colder at high altitude.» What gets thinner at high altitude? | The sun | The sea | The road | *The air
exercise: In maths, the altitude of a triangle is | The line all round the edge | *The line straight down from a corner to the opposite side, at a right angle | The number of corners | The longest side of the triangle
test: «When a plane gains altitude, it is going higher.» What is the plane doing when it gains altitude? | Landing on the ground | Going lower | Stopping its engines | *Going higher
test: The hikers felt dizzy and sick near the top of the mountain. Their teacher said they had altitude sickness. What does that mean? | Feeling sleepy after lunch | Being sick on a boat | A cold caught in winter | *Feeling unwell because they were very high up
exam: Sam says the altitude of a triangle is its longest side. Is he right? | *No, altitude is the height, the line straight down from a corner at a right angle | Yes, it is the line all round the edge | No, altitude is the number of corners | Yes, the longest side is always the altitude
